---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["How long does it take for a DMARC record to take effect?", "DNS propagation is fast (minutes on Cloudflare), but mailbox providers cache the policy. Changes typically take effect within 24-48 hours."], ["What if I already have a DMARC record?", "Edit the existing record to update the policy or add rua=. Do not create a second record: only one DMARC record per domain is valid."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "How to Create a DMARC Record",
  description: "How to create a DMARC record: step by step with correct v=DMARC1 syntax for Cloudflare, Namecheap and GoDaddy.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "How to Create a DMARC Record" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to Create a DMARC Record: Step-by-Step Guide with Correct Syntax"
  description="How to create a DMARC record: step by step with correct v=DMARC1 syntax for Cloudflare, Namecheap and GoDaddy."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">How to Create a DMARC Record</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Create a DMARC Record</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">How to create a DMARC record: step by step with correct v=DMARC1 syntax for Cloudflare, Namecheap and GoDaddy.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Step</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>1</td><td>Go to your DNS provider (Cloudflare, Namecheap, GoDaddy)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>2</td><td>Add a TXT record with name: _dmarc.yourdomain.com (or _dmarc for root)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>3</td><td>Set the value: v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:you@yourdomain.com</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>4</td><td>Wait 24-48 hours for aggregate reports to arrive</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>5</td><td>Read the reports, fix legitimate senders, then advance to quarantine and reject</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>A DMARC record is created by adding a DNS TXT record at _dmarc.yourdomain.com that starts with v=DMARC1 and defines the policy and reporting configuration for email authentication.</p><p class='mt-3'>The p= tag controls what happens to mail that fails authentication: none (deliver normally, monitor only), quarantine (deliver to spam), or reject (bounce).</p><p class='mt-3'>The rua= tag specifies the email address where mailbox providers send daily aggregate reports, which are essential for identifying all legitimate sending sources before advancing the policy.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The mistake I see most often: publishing p=reject immediately without checking DMARC reports first. This bounces legitimate email from services you forgot about (billing systems, CRM tools, notification services). Always start at p=none and advance based on data.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take for a DMARC record to take effect?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">DNS propagation is fast (minutes on Cloudflare), but mailbox providers cache the policy. Changes typically take effect within 24-48 hours.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What if I already have a DMARC record?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Edit the existing record to update the policy or add rua=. Do not create a second record: only one DMARC record per domain is valid.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
